好吧，现在达里尔知道自己的处境了，因为瓦尔在关于她男朋友的事上撒了谎。

1271
00:54:51.540 --> 00:54:53.140
And it was a love beanie.
而且那是一顶爱心针织帽。

1272
00:54:53.980 --> 00:54:55.940
Val, what is going on?
瓦尔，到底怎么回事？

1273
00:54:56.340 --> 00:54:56.680
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1274
00:54:57.380 --> 00:55:03.260
Dwight has cleaned out the conference room now of all of his weird Florida stuff.
德怀特现在已经把会议室里那些奇怪的佛罗里达玩意儿都清理干净了。

1275
00:55:03.660 --> 00:55:07.640
And he's going to have a real meeting because no one dropped out.
他打算开一场真正的会议，因为没人中途退出。

1276
00:55:07.760 --> 00:55:08.540
Here's his team.
这是他的团队。

1277
00:55:08.720 --> 00:55:09.900
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1278
00:55:10.320 --> 00:55:11.880
People surprise him.
大家给了他惊喜。

1279
00:55:12.060 --> 00:55:13.300
They are eager.
他们很积极。

1280
00:55:13.560 --> 00:55:14.380
They are engaged.
他们很投入。

1281
00:55:14.660 --> 00:55:16.220
They're presenting good ideas.
他们提出了很好的点子。

1282
00:55:16.920 --> 00:55:17.480
Yeah.
是啊。

1283
00:55:17.820 --> 00:55:19.020
Dwight is coming around.
德怀特开始转变态度了。

1284
00:55:19.020 --> 00:55:19.860
He's like, you know what?
他心想，你知道吗？

1285
00:55:19.860 --> 00:55:22.640
Maybe this isn't such a bad team after all.
也许这个团队其实并没有那么糟糕。

1286
00:55:22.920 --> 00:55:24.100
Perfect and schlock.
完美与劣质。

1287
00:55:24.320 --> 00:55:26.080
I loved this conference room scene.
我很喜欢这场会议室的戏。

1288
00:55:26.260 --> 00:55:27.340
It warmed my heart.
它温暖了我的心。

1289
00:55:27.480 --> 00:55:27.880
Me too.
我也是。

1290
00:55:28.240 --> 00:55:29.640
I'm excited for them.
我为他们感到兴奋。

1291
00:55:29.820 --> 00:55:32.260
I loved how earnest and excited everyone was.
我喜欢每个人那种真诚又兴奋的样子。

1292
00:55:33.220 --> 00:55:38.340
Erin is going to have a talking head where she says she's going to Florida and she's not coming back.
艾琳会有一个采访镜头，她说她要去佛罗里达，而且不会再回来了。

1293
00:55:38.640 --> 00:55:38.980
Oof.
哎哟。

1294
00:55:39.640 --> 00:55:41.580
Miles McNutt really liked that talking head.
迈尔斯·麦克纳特真的很喜欢那个采访镜头。

1295
00:55:41.760 --> 00:55:45.540
He liked that Erin was doing this for other reasons.
他喜欢艾琳是因为其他原因才这么做的。

1296
00:55:46.260 --> 00:55:46.780
Yeah.
是啊。

1297
00:55:47.460 --> 00:55:50.100
Again, you can't go there with logic.
再说一次，你不能用逻辑去衡量这件事。

1298
00:55:50.280 --> 00:55:50.860
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1299
00:55:51.020 --> 00:55:57.860
Like why Sabre would put together this specific team of people for this specific project.
比如为什么赛博公司会为了这个特定的项目组建这个特定的人员团队。

1300
00:55:58.680 --> 00:55:59.200
Yes.
是的。

1301
00:55:59.320 --> 00:56:02.620
It makes no sense that we need both Erin and Kathy.
我们需要艾琳和凯西两个人，这根本说不通。

1302
00:56:02.880 --> 00:56:03.320
Yes.
没错。

1303
00:56:03.480 --> 00:56:04.600
Two admins.
两个行政人员。

1304
00:56:04.860 --> 00:56:05.120
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1305
00:56:05.200 --> 00:56:07.100
One of whom is not a permanent employee.
其中一个还不是正式员工。

1306
00:56:07.340 --> 00:56:07.800
That's right.
确实如此。

1307
00:56:07.800 --> 00:56:15.260
In fact, if they did let Kathy go since Pam has come back, they would be recouping that salary.
事实上，如果他们在帕姆回来后就辞退凯西，他们就能省下那笔工资。

1308
00:56:16.320 --> 00:56:16.480
True.
确实。

1309
00:56:17.040 --> 00:56:18.220
Can't go there, Miles.
不能谈这个，迈尔斯。

1310
00:56:18.440 --> 00:56:19.240
We can't go there.
我们不能谈这个。

1311
00:56:21.500 --> 00:56:26.320
This episode ends with the Florida group getting into a van for the airport.
这一集结尾时，佛罗里达小组坐上一辆面包车前往机场。

1312
00:56:26.640 --> 00:56:27.640
Everyone's saying goodbye.
大家都在道别。

1313
00:56:28.100 --> 00:56:28.720
Wait, wait.
等等，等等。

1314
00:56:28.860 --> 00:56:29.800
Kathy's on the phone.
凯西在打电话。

1315
00:56:30.520 --> 00:56:30.840
Yeah.
是啊。

1316
00:56:31.020 --> 00:56:33.920
She's talking to her friend on a bench.
她坐在长椅上和朋友聊天。

1317
00:56:34.060 --> 00:56:34.280
Yeah.
是啊。

1318
00:56:34.440 --> 00:56:36.200
She says all expenses paid.
她说所有费用全包。

1319
00:56:36.500 --> 00:56:37.020
Yeah.
是啊。

1320
00:56:37.300 --> 00:56:38.140
Jim's going to be there.
吉姆也会去那里。

1321
00:56:38.700 --> 00:56:40.240
Their marriage is not good.
他们的婚姻状况不太好。

1322
00:56:40.760 --> 00:56:42.320
Nobody knows better than me.
没人比我更清楚了。

1323
00:56:43.100 --> 00:56:44.360
Definitely we will.
我们肯定会去的。

1324
00:56:44.720 --> 00:56:46.620
It's three weeks in Tallahassee.
要在塔拉哈西待三周。

1325
00:56:46.760 --> 00:56:47.960
What else is there to do?
还能做什么呢？

1326
00:56:49.500 --> 00:56:51.040
So, dun-dun-dun.
所以，当当当。

1327
00:56:52.120 --> 00:56:54.160
Guess who didn't care for this talking head?
猜猜谁不喜欢这段采访？

1328
00:56:54.300 --> 00:56:54.480
Who?
谁？

1329
00:56:54.960 --> 00:56:57.100
Sydney in Charlotte, North Carolina.
北卡罗来纳州夏洛特的悉尼。

1330
00:56:57.360 --> 00:56:58.340
What you got, Sydney?
悉尼，你有什么看法？

1331
00:56:58.340 --> 00:57:05.200
Sydney wrote in and said, the ending of this episode, dot, dot, dot, Kathy, boo.
悉尼写信来说，这一集的结尾，省略号，凯西，嘘。

1332
00:57:06.760 --> 00:57:09.300
The start of this new Jim Kathy storyline.
这个吉姆和凯西新剧情线的开端。

1333
00:57:09.740 --> 00:57:15.480
How did you guys, Jenna especially, feel about this whole, quote, new girl tries to steal Jim's
你们，尤其是珍娜，对于这个所谓的“新女孩试图勾引吉姆”的剧情线感觉如何？

1334
00:57:15.480 --> 00:57:15.880
storyline?
剧情线？

1335
00:57:16.540 --> 00:57:21.380
I get that Jim and Pam need conflict, but it's gross, and I just don't like Kathy at all,
我明白吉姆和帕姆需要冲突，但这很恶心，我一点也不喜欢凯西，

1336
00:57:21.460 --> 00:57:25.760
and I feel bad because I'm sure the actress is very nice, but she had to play such an icky
我感到很抱歉，因为我相信这位女演员本人一定很好，但她不得不扮演这样一个令人讨厌的

1337
00:57:25.760 --> 00:57:26.300
character.
角色。

1338
00:57:27.180 --> 00:57:31.740
Well, Sydney, how I felt about it was that I didn't feel like we earned it, Sydney.
嗯，悉尼，我的感受是，我觉得我们并没有铺垫好，悉尼。

1339
00:57:31.960 --> 00:57:36.040
I didn't think we earned this moment on the bench for this character of Kathy.
我不认为我们为凯西这个角色在长椅上的这一刻做好了铺垫。

1340
00:57:36.040 --> 00:57:44.180
We hadn't seen her look at Jim, pine away for Jim, be interested in Jim, and now all of a
我们之前没见过她注视吉姆、为吉姆神魂颠倒、对吉姆感兴趣，结果现在突然之间，

1341
00:57:44.180 --> 00:57:47.280
sudden she thinks she's going to have an affair with him.
她就觉得要和他发生一段婚外情了。

1342
00:57:47.400 --> 00:57:49.120
It makes her seem delusional.
这让她看起来像是有妄想症。

1343
00:57:50.040 --> 00:57:52.860
Yeah, well, they took out so much that they wrote for her.
是啊，好吧，他们删减了很多为她写的戏份。

1344
00:57:52.860 --> 00:57:55.580
That would have been a slower build to this moment.
那些戏份本可以让这一刻的到来更循序渐进。

1345
00:57:56.840 --> 00:58:04.500
I believe that someone Kathy's age and in that office could be enamored with Jim.
我相信像凯西那个年纪、在那个办公室里的人，确实可能会迷恋吉姆。

1346
00:58:04.740 --> 00:58:05.120
Sure.
当然。

1347
00:58:05.260 --> 00:58:08.300
Have a type of, like, emotional crush on him.
对他产生一种类似情感上的迷恋。

1348
00:58:08.460 --> 00:58:08.820
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1349
00:58:09.080 --> 00:58:14.320
I could see where Jim might like the attention even if he doesn't realize he does.
我能理解吉姆为什么会享受这种关注，即使他自己并没有意识到。

1350
00:58:14.560 --> 00:58:15.920
But none of that happened.
但这一切都没有发生。

1351
00:58:15.920 --> 00:58:18.280
I know, because it's all cut out.
我知道，因为全都被剪掉了。

1352
00:58:19.160 --> 00:58:22.400
So it does seem out of absolute left field.
所以这看起来确实非常突兀。

1353
00:58:22.620 --> 00:58:22.880
Yeah.
没错。

1354
00:58:23.640 --> 00:58:25.040
That's how I felt about it.
我当时也是这种感觉。

1355
00:58:25.080 --> 00:58:25.260
Yeah.
是啊。

1356
00:58:25.400 --> 00:58:26.200
It didn't feel earned.
感觉铺垫不够。

1357
00:58:26.400 --> 00:58:29.460
And then as for what's going to happen, we'll get to it.
至于接下来会发生什么，我们稍后会讲到。

1358
00:58:29.560 --> 00:58:30.560
We'll get to it.
我们会讲到的。

1359
00:58:30.700 --> 00:58:32.440
Well, that was Special Project.
好了，以上就是《特别项目》的内容。

1360
00:58:32.720 --> 00:58:35.580
You guys, thanks so much for sending in your questions and comments.
各位，非常感谢你们发来的问题和评论。

1361
00:58:35.780 --> 00:58:40.240
Thank you, Steve Burgess, for getting back to me about a few of those tidbits I was wondering about.
感谢史蒂夫·伯吉斯回复了我关于那几个小细节的疑问。

1362
00:58:40.800 --> 00:58:42.920
I'm going to put on my zipper earrings.
我要戴上我的拉链耳环了。

1363
00:58:43.180 --> 00:58:43.640
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1364
00:58:43.680 --> 00:58:46.880
I'm going to walk out of here feeling like fashionable mom.
我要以时尚辣妈的姿态走出这里了。

1365
00:58:47.060 --> 00:58:48.560
And we'll see you next week.
我们下周见。

1366
00:58:48.720 --> 00:58:49.740
We'll see you then.
到时候见。

1367
00:58:49.920 --> 00:58:51.080
We hope you have a great one.
祝大家过得愉快。

1368
00:58:55.230 --> 00:58:57.210
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1369
00:58:57.530 --> 00:59:01.630
Office Ladies is produced by Earwolf, Jenna Fisher, and Angela Kinsey.
《办公室女士》由Earwolf、珍娜·费舍和安吉拉·金赛制作。

1370
00:59:01.830 --> 00:59:04.010
Our senior producer is Cassie Jerkins.
我们的高级制作人是卡西·杰金斯。

1371
00:59:04.230 --> 00:59:06.270
Our in-studio engineer is Sam Kiefer.
我们的演播室工程师是萨姆·基弗。

1372
00:59:06.490 --> 00:59:08.670
Our editing and mixing engineer is Jordan Duffy.
我们的剪辑和混音工程师是乔丹·达菲。

1373
00:59:08.850 --> 00:59:11.010
And our associate producer is Ainsley Bubaco.
我们的助理制作人是安斯利·布巴科。

1374
00:59:11.010 --> 00:59:14.190
Our theme song is Rubber Tree by Creed Bratton.
我们的主题曲是克里德·布拉顿创作的《橡胶树》。
